From 3721a93b0e2b6c9c93cb1e5cf7b7b553d652b7da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:43:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 85/86] XHTTP: Fixes and costs from the last review items of
 the flow governor

A guard probe that found another still queued behind a write was
dropped and yet noted as sent, holding the periodic PINGs back for 10 s;
it now leaves the queued one to answer. Read and Write take their
scratch buffers from a pool of pointers, which allocates nothing where
putting a slice back did each call, and read the clock once per call
when a frame needs it, not on every frame boundary: on the benchmarks
Read takes 5% and Write 6% less time, with no allocations left.
currentRTT and floorConfirmed share one check of the kernel's floor.
Comments say which lock guards what, that the client queues nothing,
what bounds the window a cap shows, and are wrapped.
